      "description": "Faculty Positions | Queen's University Cookie Disclosure Queen's University uses cookies to provide the best possible online experience. Learn about our privacy practices. OK Skip to main content Skip to footer Sign In University Wide MyQueen’sU - SOLUS, MyHR, and more Microsoft 365 Outlook on the web - Email onQ Research–Service Portal: Cayuse and TRAQ Course Reserves Web Proxy Change password / Manage NetID Faculty/School Portals Business - Program Portals Grad Studies – Faculty and Staff Portal Health Sciences - Elentra Law - QLaw Smith Engineering Intranet Faculty Positions Faculty Positions Now Available The university invites applications from all qualified individuals Queen’s is committed to employment equity and diversity in the workplace and welcomes applications from Black, racialized/visible minority and Indigenous people, women, persons with disabilities, and 2SLGBTQ+ persons. The university has policies in place to support employees with disabilities, including an Accommodation in the Workplace Policy and a policy on the provision of job accommodations that take into account an employee’s accessibility needs due to disability. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadians and Permanent Residents of Canada will be given priority. The university will provide support in its recruitment processes to applicants with disabilities, including accommodation that takes into account an applicant’s accessibility needs. Learn more: Immigration and Relocation See Also: 2025/26 Queen's National Scholar (QNS)Positions Available Though many of the application deadlines noted below have passed, the competitions will remain open until the position has been filled. Faculty of Arts and Science Expand All Collapse All Tenure-track positions Open Collapsible Close Collapsible School of Computing Computational Intelligence - Application Deadline: September 26, 2025 Educational Sc