    "https://educ.queensu.ca/about/work": {
      "title": "Work",
      "description": "Work at Queen's | Faculty of Education Cookie Disclosure Queen's University uses cookies to provide the best possible online experience. Learn about our privacy practices. OK Skip to main content Skip to footer Sign In University Wide MyQueen’sU - SOLUS, MyHR, and more Microsoft 365 Outlook on the web - Email onQ Research–Service Portal: Cayuse and TRAQ Course Reserves Web Proxy Change password / Manage NetID Faculty/School Portals Business - Program Portals Grad Studies – Faculty and Staff Portal Health Sciences - Elentra Law - QLaw Smith Engineering Intranet Faculty of Education Main menu Megamenu Teacher Ed Down arrow Getting Started Concurrent Education Consecutive (BEd) Down arrow Technological Education Program Tracks Down arrow Artist in Community Education Indigenous Teacher Education Program Outdoor & Experiential Education Primary-Junior French as a Second Language Multi-Session Programs Down arrow Indigenous Teacher Education Program (Community-Based) Primary-Junior French as a Second Language Multi-Session Technological Education Multi-Session Program Continuing Teacher Education Down arrow ABQs/AQs Post-Graduate Certificates for Internationally Trained Teachers Post-Graduate Certificates Graduate Down arrow On-Campus Down arrow Master of Education (MEd) Doctor of Philosophy in Education Online Down arrow Graduate Diploma in Education (GDE) Professional Master of Education (PME) Ladder your credentials Blended Program Down arrow Master of Education in World Indigenous Studies in Education (WISE) Community Down arrow Alumni Down arrow Alumni News Careers Beyond the Classroom Grad Alumni News Community Initiatives Down arrow Ever Scholar Sistema Kingston Giving Host a Placement or Internship Indigenous Relations International Connections Student Experiences Down arrow Gender and Sexualities Alliance Teacher Candidates of Colour Transgender and/or Gender-Non-conforming FAQs Current Students Down arrow ConEd Students Down arrow ConEd Degree Requirements ConEd Supports and Services Regulations and Policies Teacher Candidates Down arrow Academic Calendar Awards Course Descriptions Regulations and Policies Supports for Teacher Candidates on Practicum TC Supports & Services Graduate Students Down arrow Academic Calendar Grad - Supports & Services Grad Office Resources Down arrow Event Calendar Indigenous Education Supports Student Services Office Research Down arrow Overview Research Profiles Ethics Events & Publications Down arrow Knowledge Forum RBJSE Research Newsletter Centre for Community Engagement and Social Change Research Groups For Teachers Down arrow Podcast: Popular Podagogy AI in the Classroom International Teaching and Practicum Practicum Information Teaching Resources About Down arrow About Down arrow Our Deans Academic Plan Equity & Diversity Faculty Board News Down arrow Media Releases Event Calendar Work With Us Duncan McArthur Hall Down arrow Construction Updates Maps Room Reservations Continuing Education, Professional, & Global Programs Down arrow Continuing Teacher Education Professional Studies School of English Site Illustrations Contact Us Down arrow Contact Us People Directory Hire our Graduates Down arrow Options Career Fair Supports Down arrow Technology and Facilities Services Personal Counsellors About - Tsi Nahò:ten - E Teg Work at Queen's Work at Queen's Explore teaching opportunities with our Faculty of Education The University invites applications from all qualified individuals. Queen's is committed to employment equity, diversity, and inclusion in the workplace and welcomes applications from black, racialized/visible minority and Indigenous peoples, women and persons with disabilities and 2SLGBTQ+ persons. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, in accordance with Canadian Immigration requirements, Canadian citizens and Permanent Residents of Canada will be given priority. To comply with Federal laws, the University is obliged to gather statistical information about how many applicants for each job vacancy are Canadian citizens / permanent residents of Canada. Applicants need not identify their country of origin or citizenship, however, all applications must include one of the following statements: “I am a Canadian citizen / permanent resident of Canada”; OR, “I am not a Canadian citizen / permanent resident of Canada”. Applications that do not include this information will be deemed incomplete. The University will provide support in its recruitment processes to applicants with disabilities, including accommodation that takes into account an applicant’s accessibility needs. If you require accommodation during this process, please contact edudeans@queensu.ca . Academic staff at Queen’s University are governed by a Collective Agreement (2022-2025) between the Queen’s University Faculty Association (QUFA) and the University which is available online at the Faculty Relations Office website and on the QUFA website . Types of Teaching Positions Tenure Track Tenure Track positions are associated with job titles, such as Professor and Associate Professor. Academic tenure is primarily intended to guarantee the right to academic freedom. Tenure Track Positions Available Graduate Teaching Fellow (GTF) GTFs are graduate students who serve as the sole instructor of a Bachelor of Education course. The GTF is responsible for all aspects of curriculum and assessment. Most fellowship nominations are adjudicated by the Fellowship Committee of the School of Graduate Studies through annual competitions. Others are administered by departments. Graduate Teaching Fellow (GTF) Positions Available Postdoctoral Fellowships Postdoctoral Fellows (PDFs) are valued members of the Queen's community and make an indispensable contribution to the research environment of the University. As trained researchers, they have the opportunity to make a significant contribution to their chosen field. As members of a research group, they can form partnerships with faculty researchers and can guide graduate students. Postdoctoral Fellowship Postings Term Adjunct Term adjuncts with and without benefits are instructors with a limited-term faculty appointment of one term to three years in duration and with a limited range of academic responsibilities (e.g., instruction/evaluation, coordination/administration). For questions about the term adjunct postings, please contact: employment.education@queensu.ca . Application packages, with all required documentation, should be sent to the email address identified in the application section of each job posting. Term Adjunct Positions Available Teaching Assistants Teaching Assistants are graduate students (MEd and PhD candidates). They are supervised by one instructor and are assigned to assist the professor during his/her course. The professor and Teaching Assistant sign the Queen’s Teaching Assistant Agreement Form which outlines the total number of hours for which the Teaching Assistant is to be paid (total number of hours per term is 100) and the allocation of those hours by duties/responsibilities. Some duties/responsibilities include: a) lecturing, b) marking assignments, c) attending classes, and d) regular meetings with course instructors. New Teaching Assistants are required to take a three hour introductory training workshop. They are financed through the Faculty of Education. Teaching Assistantship Postings Expand All Collapse All Resources for Work and Life at Queen's and in Kingston Open Collapsible Close Collapsible Queen’s is one of Canada’s most prestigious and innovative universities located in one of the country’s most appealing cities – Kingston, Ontario. The University is known for the quality of its programs; its active and high-achieving student body; its vibrant, residential community; and its international opportunities. Queen's is one of the country’s top-ranked institutions and has a global reputation for scholarship, research, social purpose, spirit, and diversity. Queen’s University Faculty Recruitment and Support Queen’s Human Resources Queen's Unions and Associations Kingston, situated at the eastern end of Lake Ontario, is midway between Toronto, Montreal, and Ottawa. The beautiful and historic Thousand Islands region is at its doorstep, as is the bridge crossing the St. Lawrence River to the USA. It is easy to work, live, and travel in Kingston where there are abundant opportunities for cultural, recreational, and leisure activities. Live & Work in Kingston City of Kingston Mandatory Training for Employees Open Collapsible Close Collapsible As part of government mandated regulations, all employees of the University are required to complete the following training modules. University employees include: faculty members, staff, graduate teaching fellows, teaching assistants and casual staff. Equity Training There are four training components that are mandatory for all Queen’s employees: 1. Environmental Health and Safety Awareness Training (1.5 hours) Available here: www.queensu.ca/risk/safety/training/health-safety-awareness 2. Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act Training (3.5 hours). Modules to complete are: a. Accessible Customer Service b. Access Forward c. HR101 d. Accessible Instruction for Educators (faculty, GTFs, and TAs only) Available here: www.queensu.ca/hreo/education/mytraining-record 3. Sexual Violence Training, “It Takes All of Us” (1 hour) Available here: www.queensu.ca/sexualviolencesupport/it-takes-all-us 4. Anti-Racism Training, \"Building a Foundation for Change at Queen's\" (45 minutes) Available here: https://www.queensu.ca/hreo/anti-racism-building-foundation-change-queens All modules for training are available online with your NetID through the applicable Queen’s University website and should be completed within one month of your appointment commencing. Visit the NetID Profile Manager webpage to activate your Net ID. If you do not remember if you have already completed the training, you can review your training record via mytrainingrecord , and any outstanding mandatory training will be listed under ‘Trainings Still Required’. Staff Positions The Faculty employs approximately 60 staff members, including administrative assistants, coordinators, and managers, as well as instructional designers and technical support staff. Staff positions are advertised on the Queen’s Human Resources website . Faculty of Education Duncan McArthur Hall 511 Union Street Kingston, ON K7M 5R7 Canada Tel: (613) 533-6205 Faculty of Education on Facebook Faculty of Education on Instagram Faculty of Education on LinkedIn Faculty of Education on Youtube Footer menu Equity & Diversity Library Room Reservations Footer Menu 2 Make a Gift Webmail onQ Web Privacy Queen’s University is situated on the territory of the Haudenosaunee and Anishinaabek . © 2026 Queen’s University"
    },
