      "title": "Faculty Publications",
      "description": "Faculty Publications | School of Religion Cookie Disclosure Queen's University uses cookies to provide the best possible online experience. Learn about our privacy practices. OK Skip to main content Skip to footer Sign In University Wide MyQueen’sU - SOLUS, MyHR, and more Microsoft 365 Outlook on the web - Email onQ Research–Service Portal: Cayuse and TRAQ Course Reserves Web Proxy Change password / Manage NetID Faculty/School Portals Business - Program Portals Grad Studies – Faculty and Staff Portal Health Sciences - Elentra Law - QLaw Smith Engineering Intranet School of Religion Main navigation Home Undergraduate Down arrow Undergraduate Overview Degree Programs & Plans Current Course Offerings RELS Courses at a Glance RELS Courses as Electives Departmental Student Council Student Forms Quick Links FAQs Graduate Down arrow Graduate Overview MA Program Admission Requirements Application Process Funding and Awards Current Course Offerings Graduate Supervision Resources for Graduate Students Our Students People Down arrow People Overview Administration Faculty Down arrow Faculty Overview Amarnath Amarasingam Richard S. Ascough Dustin Atlas Danielle LaGrone Jennifer S. Leath Jorge Legoas P. Sharday C. Mosurinjohn Aditi Sen Tracy J. Trothen M. Shobhana Xavier Emeritus and Retired Faculty Postdoctoral Fellows Down arrow Postdoctoral Fellows Overview Teaching Fellows Down arrow Teaching Fellows Overview Research Down arrow Research Overview Faculty Publications Religion, Gender, Sexuality and Youth Down arrow Religion, Gender, Sexuality and Youth Overview Project Aims Research Team Advisory Committee Results Contact Alumni Down arrow Alumni Overview Alumni Profiles News & Events Down arrow News & Events Overview News Events Employment Opportunities Contact Research Faculty Publications Faculty Publications The award-winning faculty at the School of Religion undertake academic research into the religions and cultures of the world and religious issues emerging in the Canadian landscape, and have research links to universities globally. Teaching and research range over some of the major religious traditions, including Buddhism, Christianity, Confucianism, Daoism, Hinduism, Islam, and Judaism, and focus on key geographic regions such as China, Europe, India, the Middle East, and North America. In the past few years, faculty research and publications have included: Forough Jahanbakhsh : The Expansion of Prophetic Experience: Essays on Historicity, Contingency and Plurality in Religion (edited, 2009); Islam, Democracy and Religious Modernism in Iran 1953-2000: From Bazargan to Soroush (2001) Ellen Goldberg : Bollywood Horrors: Religion, Violence and Cinematic Fears in Indian Film (e dited by Aditi Sen and Brian Collins, 2022); Gurus of Modern Yoga (edited with Mark Singleton, 2014); Associations in the Greco-Roman World: A Sourcebook (with Philip A. Harland and John S. Kloppenborg, 2012) James Miller : China's Green Religion: Daoism and the Quest for a Sustainable Future (2017); Religion and Ecological Sustainability in China (edited with Dan Smyer Yu and Peter van der Veer, 2014) Pamela Dickey Young : Women and Religious Traditions (edited with Leona Anderson, 3rd edition, 2015); Religion and Sexuality: Diversity and the Limits of Tolerance (edited with Heather Shipley and Tracy Trothen, 2015); Religion, Sex and Politics: Christian Churches and Same-Sex Marriage in Canada (2012) Tracy Trothen : Winning the Race? Religion, Hope, and Reshaping the Sport Enhancement Debate (2015) ; Religion and Transhumanism: The Unknown Future of Human Enhancement (edited with Calvin Mercer, 2015) ; Shattering Illusions: Child Sexual Abuse Policies and Canadian Religious Institutions (2012) William Morrow : Protest Against God: The Eclipse of a Biblical Tradition (2006) Richard Ascough : Associations in the Greco-Roman World: A Sourcebook (with Philip A. Harland and John S. Kloppenborg, 2012); 1 and 2 Thessalonians: Encountering the Christ Group at Thessalonike (2014) Aditi Sen : Bollywood Horrors: Religion, Violence and Cinematic Fears in Indian Film (e dited by Ellen Goldberg and Brian Collins, 2022) × Previous Next Queen's School of Religion Theological Hall, Suite 211 Kingston, ON K7L 3N6 Canada Tel: 613 533 2106 School of Religion on Facebook Footer menu Campus Security Accessibility Services Accessibility Services Wellness Services Student Wellness Services Web Privacy Queen’s University is situated on the territory of the Haudenosaunee and Anishinaabek . © 2026 Queen’s University"
    },
