    "https://www.queensu.ca/religion/teaching-fellow-position-available-winter-2024": {
      "title": "Teaching Fellow Position Available –Winter 2024",
      "description": "Teaching Fellow Position Available –Winter 2024 | School of Religion Cookie Disclosure Queen's University uses cookies to provide the best possible online experience. Learn about our privacy practices. OK Skip to main content Skip to footer Sign In University Wide MyQueen’sU - SOLUS, MyHR, and more Microsoft 365 Outlook on the web - Email onQ Research–Service Portal: Cayuse and TRAQ Course Reserves Web Proxy Change password / Manage NetID Faculty/School Portals Business - Program Portals Grad Studies – Faculty and Staff Portal Health Sciences - Elentra Law - QLaw Smith Engineering Intranet School of Religion Main navigation Home Undergraduate Down arrow Undergraduate Overview Degree Programs & Plans Current Course Offerings RELS Courses at a Glance RELS Courses as Electives Departmental Student Council Student Forms Quick Links FAQs Graduate Down arrow Graduate Overview MA Program Admission Requirements Application Process Funding and Awards Current Course Offerings Graduate Supervision Resources for Graduate Students Our Students People Down arrow People Overview Administration Faculty Down arrow Faculty Overview Amarnath Amarasingam Richard S. Ascough Dustin Atlas Danielle LaGrone Jennifer S. Leath Jorge Legoas P. Sharday C. Mosurinjohn Aditi Sen Tracy J. Trothen M. Shobhana Xavier Emeritus and Retired Faculty Postdoctoral Fellows Down arrow Postdoctoral Fellows Overview Teaching Fellows Down arrow Teaching Fellows Overview Research Down arrow Research Overview Faculty Publications Religion, Gender, Sexuality and Youth Down arrow Religion, Gender, Sexuality and Youth Overview Project Aims Research Team Advisory Committee Results Contact Alumni Down arrow Alumni Overview Alumni Profiles News & Events Down arrow News & Events Overview News Events Employment Opportunities Contact Teaching Fellow Position Available –Winter 2024 Mar 21, 2023 The School of Religion at Queen’s University invites applications from suitably qualified graduate students at Queen’s University interested in teaching a course in Religion and Sex (RELS 236) as a Teaching Fellow. This is an on-campus lecture course with an expected enrolment of ~95 undergraduate students. This is a Winter term appointment for the period January 1 to April 30, 2024 with classes in session from January 8, 2024 to April 8, 2024. Applications should include a curriculum vitae, an unofficial transcript of graduate coursework, letters of reference from two (2) referees, as well as any other relevant materials the candidate wishes to submit for consideration such as a letter of intent, teaching dossier, or student evaluations. Applications and supporting letters sent directly to: Adnan A. Husain, Director School of Religion, Queen’s University Kingston, ON, Canada K7L 3N6 school.of.religion@queensu.ca Please arrange to have applications will be received until March 30, 2023. Review of applications will commence shortly thereafter, and the final appointment is subject to budgetary approval. Additional information about the School of Religion can be found at http://www.queensu.ca/religion. Job Description Here Article Category Employment Opportunities News Queen's School of Religion Theological Hall, Suite 211 Kingston, ON K7L 3N6 Canada Tel: 613 533 2106 School of Religion on Facebook Footer menu Campus Security Accessibility Services Accessibility Services Wellness Services Student Wellness Services Web Privacy Queen’s University is situated on the territory of the Haudenosaunee and Anishinaabek . © 2026 Queen’s University"
    },
    "http://flux.cs.queensu.ca/applying-for-a-teaching-fellow-position/": {
      "title": "Queen's School of Computing",
      "description": "Queen's School of Computing Skip to main content (Press Enter) Outlook MyQueensU onQ Toggle navigation About Contact Us 557 Goodwin Hall Queen's University Kingston, Ontario, Canada K7L 2N8 Phone: (613) 533-6050 Give to Computing The School Student Life Outreach EDII Events Sep 11 Distinguished Lecture (DL): Beyond Classical Scaling: Quantum Computing for the Next Generation of HPC 10:00am - 11:00am News Help us build the Tom Bradshaw Museum of Computing Dr. Kai Salomaa Recognized at CIAA2026 Queen’s Hosts CIAA and DCFS 2026 Ahmed Hassan to Speak at Inaugural ACM AI Leadership Summit Wendy Powley Receives A. Nico Habermann Award Testimonials ...fantastic peers, an inspiring faculty, challenging problems, and an overall feeling of community. -- Andrew Dickinson Undergraduate Fundamental Computation Artificial Intelligence Security Software Design Computing, Mathematics and Analytics Computing and the Creative Arts Questions? The School of Computing has a group of academic advisors who are here to answer your questions about our undergraduate programs. Email the QSC Undergraduate Academic Advising Team All Programs Timeline Apply Enrolment News Courses Learning Outcomes Finances Professional Internships Research Academic Advising FAQ How Can We Help? Graduate Master's (MSc) Program Doctoral (PhD) Program Biomedical Informatics Program Digilians Graduate Program (MSc) Dual Master’s Program with AUS Master of Digital Product Management (opens in a new window) Field of Study in Artificial Intelligence NSERC CREATE Program in Medical Informatics (opens in a new window) Questions? The School of Computing has a team of people who are here to help prospective students with their concerns. Email the QSC Graduate Program Team Apply Courses Finances Academic Policies Defense Procedures FAQ How Can We Help? QGCS Graduate Handbook Research Theory of Computation Software Engineering Human Computer Interaction and Gaming Artificial Intelligence Systems and Networks Data Analytics Security Biomedical Computing Questions? Our research office is here to help with your inquiries. Email the QSC Research Office Research Faculty Research Groups Seminars Technical Reports Field of Study in Artificial Intelligence NSERC CREATE Cybersecurity Program (opens in a new window) NSERC CREATE Program in Medical Informatics (opens in a new window) Queen's Centre for Security and Privacy (opens in a new window) People Director Hossam Hassanein Manager Robin Tippett Tech Ops Manager Ben Hall Undergraduate Chair Yuanzhu Chen Graduate Chair Kai Salomaa Faculty and Instructors Cross-Appointed Faculty Admin Staff Tech Staff Research Adjuncts Research Staff View All People Submit Search Highlights AI in the School of Computing Artificial Intelligence (AI) has been a core strength of the School of Computing for many years. Find out more. Queen's Centre for Security and Privacy Fostering collaboration between academia, business, and government to protect Canadians from cyberattacks. Professional Graduate Programs in Biomedical Informatics Learn How AI and Big Data Can Transform Your Career in Healthcare NSERC CREATE Training Program in Medical Informatics Preparing Canada's workforce for the health data of tomorrow. Apply today. Previous Highlight Next Highlight News Help us build the Tom Bradshaw Museum of Computing Dr. Kai Salomaa Recognized at CIAA2026 Queen’s Hosts CIAA and DCFS 2026 Ahmed Hassan to Speak at Inaugural ACM AI Leadership Summit Wendy Powley Receives A. Nico Habermann Award More News Events Sep 11 Distinguished Lecture (DL): Beyond Classical Scaling: Quantum Computing for the Next Generation of HPC 10:00am - 11:00am More Events Want your news or event featured here? Let us know! Undergraduate Studies Programs The School of Computing offers a number of undergraduate degrees to choose from. With options and specializations spanning multiple disciplines, something will match your interests. Specializations and Options Courses Apply Artificial Intelligence Learn how the human mind works and develop computational algorithms to create machine intelligence with the our programs. Computing Major with Artificial Intelligence Option Cognitive Science Specialization Questions? Concerns? Planning and executing your degree can be a bit tricky at times. We have some resources for you. Academic Advisors FAQ How Can We Help? Graduate Studies Programs All graduate students in research programs receive minimum guaranteed funding from the School of Computing, so pursuing a graduate degree does not require student debt. You can also apply with a degree in another field if you have sufficient background and/or education in Computing. Graduate studies can work for you. Master's PhD FAQ Research Explore fascinating topics and pursue your ideas with the School of Computing's eminent faculty. They conduct research in a myriad of fields and their work is recognized worldwide. Research Faculty Research Groups Specialized Programs Earn a unique graduate degree in one of our innovative programs. They offer training for graduate students and postdoctoral fellows who wish to pursue a career in an interdisciplinary field. Artificial Intelligence (Vector Scholarship) Biomedical Informatics NSERC CREATE in Cybersecurity (opens in a new window) NSERC CREATE in Medical Informatics (opens in a new window) Connect With Us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Find Us on Instagram Back to top 557 Goodwin Hall Queen's University Kingston, Ontario, Canada K7L 2N8 Computing Links Internal Site Employment Opportunities Newsletter Queen's Links Queen's University Faculty of Arts and Science School of Graduate Studies and Postdoctoral Affairs Queen’s University is situated on traditional Anishinaabe and Haudenosaunee Territory (opens in a new window) . Copyright © 2026 School of Computing, Queen's University."
    },
