    "http://www.queensu.ca/facultyrecruitment/": {
      "title": "Immigration and Relocation Support",
      "description": "Employee Immigration and Relocation Support | Queen's University Cookie Disclosure Queen's University uses cookies to provide the best possible online experience. Learn about our privacy practices. OK Skip to main content Skip to footer Sign In University Wide MyQueen’sU - SOLUS, MyHR, and more Microsoft 365 Outlook on the web - Email onQ Research–Service Portal: Cayuse and TRAQ Course Reserves Web Proxy Change password / Manage NetID Faculty/School Portals Business - Program Portals Grad Studies – Faculty and Staff Portal Health Sciences - Elentra Law - QLaw Smith Engineering Intranet Immigration and Relocation Support Main navigation Home Immigration Down arrow Information for Employers Ontario Immigrant Nominee Program (OINP) Information for Employees and Postdoctoral Fellows Information for Visitors Social Insurance Number (SIN) Down arrow Social Insurance Number (SIN) Information for Employees Relocation Down arrow Relocation Overview Planning Your Move Housing Setting Up Your Household Health Care Child Care Schools and After School Activities Banking in Canada Taxes and Investment Considerations Settlement Services Employment for Spouses/Partners Driver's Licence and Vehicle Registration Getting Oriented to Campus Down arrow Orientation to Campus Resources for New Staff and Faculty Life in Kingston Down arrow Discover Kingston Cost of Living Location and Neighbourhoods Diversity, Faith, and Culture Accessibility Recreation, Volunteering, and the Arts Contact Previous Welcome Welcome Next 1 2 3 4 Home Immigration and Relocation Support Services Immigration and Relocation Support Services The Immigration and Relocation Support team advises incoming employees on their move to Kingston as they join the Queen's community. Providing immigration and relocation services demonstrates our commitment to diversity and inclusion for all. Queen’s University welcomes staff and faculty from every province and territory within Canada and around the world. Creating a diverse workforce strengthens our community and aligns with the University’s values of Truth, Responsibility, Respect, Freedom, and Wellbeing. Immigration Services Immigration Services at Queen's University provides consultation, guidance, and advice to the university community on immigration matters related to employment and to the hosting of international academics and researchers. We maintain the employer compliance regulations required by Immigration, Refugees and Citizenship Canada (IRCC) with accuracy and transparency. Learn more about immigration support: Information for employers (inviting/hiring/rehiring a foreign national) Information for new and current employees (staff/faculty/postdoctoral fellows) Information for inviting visitors (visiting undergraduate and graduate students, professors, scholars, lecturers) Relocation Services Not sure where to start learning about your prospective new community, and how you and your family can thrive here? Relocation Services at Queen's provides personalized assistance identifying and addressing your needs before, during, or after your relocation to Queen's and Kingston. Immigration and Relocation Support Richardson Hall 74 University Avenue Kingston, ON K7L 3N6 Canada Footer Office of the Provost and Vice-Principal (Academic) Office of the Vice-Principal (Culture, Equity, and Inclusion) Footer Menu 2 Accessibility Hub Human Resources Campus Map Contact Web Privacy Queen’s University is situated on the territory of the Haudenosaunee and Anishinaabek . © 2026 Queen’s University"
    },
    "https://qsoe.educ.queensu.ca/": {
      "title": "All Programs",
      "description": "Learn English | Queen's School of English — Queen's University Menu FREE English Course FREE English Test Home Programs Application & Payment Student Experience FAQ About Contact All Programs Pick your program! Do you want a Canadian cultural experience? Do you need help preparing for an exchange or degree program in English? Whatever your language-learning goal, we have a program for you! English for Academic Purposes This 12-week intensive English language program develops knowledge, skills, and strategies for academic success. It is offered three times per year in fall, winter, and summer. Canadian Academic Skills, English and Sustainability This 3-week English immersion program focuses on developing language skills using Canadian academic content and the UN\\'s Sustainable Development Goals. It emphasizes the knowledge, skills and strategies needed for academic success and is offered twice each year in early spring and summer. Canadian English Experience This 3–4 week English immersion program is ideal for those who want to immerse themselves in Canadian culture while learning English. It is offered once per year in winter. QBridge QBridge is an English language pathway for students who have been given a conditional offer of admission to a Queen\\'s University undergraduate program. Academic English Foundations This 6-week intensive English language program builds the foundational knowledge, skills, and strategies for academic success. It is offered three times per year in fall, winter, and summer. English for Beginners English for Beginners is a free 6-module online ESL course that will give you the chance to improve your English skills with some fun activities. When you finish the course, you will receive a digital badge of completion. Language Support Language Support provides weekly online tutorials for university students currently enrolled in an English-language degree or diploma program. Tutoring Our customized one-on-one virtual tutoring sessions offer personalized instruction specifically targeted to your learning needs. Pathways and Embedded Programs Queen’s School of English is proud to partner with many different parts of the University and Kingston community to provide language programming to support student journeys from English Learner to Graduate. English for Immigration and Citizenship Law Pre-Admission Program (Part-time) This part-time 2-semester, 24-week intensive English language program develops knowledge, skills, and strategies for academic success in the Queen's Faculty of Law Graduate Diploma in Immigration and Citizenship Law. English for Immigration and Citizenship Law Official Pathway (Full-time) This fall 12–week intensive English language program develops knowledge, skills, and strategies for academic success in the Queen's Faculty of Law Graduate Diploma in Immigration and Citizenship Law. It is only offered online once per year from early September to early December. Tailored Programs English for Mining This unique, six-week online course offers comprehensive training in English language skills tailored specifically for the mining sector. Advance your career in the mining industry while improving your English language skills. Join us and become part of a global community of professionals who make a difference in the mining industry. Student Experience At Queen’s School of English you will have the opportunity to extend your learning beyond the classroom. Participate in trips, activities, volunteer club and student council to make this experience your own. Immerse yourself in Canadian culture as you develop friendships, build community and create memories to last a lifetime. Guides Student Life Volunteer Club Trips Accommodation About For 80 years the Queen’s School of English has provided outstanding student support, well-researched curriculum, exceptional instruction, and a vibrant student life program. Mission, Vision, Values Queen's University, Kingston, Canada Contribution to Field Our Team Policy Application & Payment QSoE accepts many different payment types through our registration system, and we never charge application or registration fees. Application No application fees! Our payment and registration experience is made to be as simple as possible. Payment QSoE accepts many different payment types through our registration system, and we never charge application or registration fees. Refund Policy QSoE offers refunds based on how much of a program has been completed. Scholarships Competitive scholarships are available at QSoE, as well as National Scholarships. Tuition Fees QSoE fees are charged in Canadian Dollars and are charged per semester of study. Additional Fees Some additional fees will be charged to access health services and university facilities. Queen’s University uses cookies to provide the best possible online experience. Learn about our privacy practices. OK FREE English Course FREE English Test What we do For more than 80 years, Queen’s School of English has produced cutting-edge and accredited English language programs for English language learners from around the world who wish to improve their academic English within the Canadian academic context. Learn English for University at PROGRAMS PEOPLE EXPERIENCE Upcoming Dates CASES Summer 2026 Program End: September  4, 2026 EAP Fall 2026 Program Start: September 10, 2026 AEF Fall 2026 Program Start: September 10, 2026 QBRGEAP Fall 2026 Program Start: September 10, 2026 EICLF Fall 2026 Program Start: September 10, 2026 TUT Fall 2026 Program Start: September 10, 2026 EAP            Fall 2026            Program Start September 10, 2026 QBRGEAP            Fall 2026            Program Start September 10, 2026 TUT            Fall 2026            Program Start September 10, 2026 CASES            Summer 2026            Program End September  4, 2026 AEF            Fall 2026            Program Start September 10, 2026 EICLF            Fall 2026            Program Start September 10, 2026 Learn English in Canada at Queen's University From its safety and openness to diversity, to its natural landscape and modern cities, find out why Canada is one of the world’s top language study destinations for international students. With official languages of both English and French, Canada is a country which appreciates different languages and welcomes newcomers from all over the world. Canada is known internationally for its high quality of education, and so we invite you to study and develop your language skills for university at university. Queen’s is situated on traditional Anishinaabe (Ah- nish-in-ah-bay) and Haudenosaunee (Ho-den-o-show-nee) territory. Learn More Accreditation Queen's School of English a part of the Faculty of Education at Queen’s University, a Canadian Designated Learning Institution. The Faculty of Education is fully accredited by the Ontario College of Teachers for the provision of teacher education in the province of Ontario; likewise, Queen's University is member of Canada's elite U15 group of universities and qualifies students to practice across innumerable professional fields. Take our free online English test! Take our free 10-minute English test to get an idea of where your English level is just now. You will need to listen to some questions, so make sure you have headphones or a quiet area, and don’t worry if you don’t have time now – the test is available for free 365 days a year! Take QUEST Our students love Queen's School of English! QSoE is not just an institution but also a family. The teachers are very experienced and supportive of the students’ individual needs. Furthermore, the staff are very helpful in organizing school activities and helping students. You can meet new friends. Carla English for Academic Purposes I came to Kingston to learn English in a group from Shanghai. I improved my listening, reading, spoken and writing skills. I had an internship at the City of Kingston. I learned  about Canadian government, about it’s leadership management and operation. Yuhong Canadian English Experience My two sessions here have been an amazing experience. You can meet people from all over the world. It is a friendly environment and the program is well organized. Life at Queen’s residences is really cool because you can make many friends. Alberto English for Academic Purposes Through my communications with other international students we helped and encouraged each other all the time. QSoE has a great communication network between students, teachers and monitors. I especially have a feeling of gratitude towards my teachers who tried to understand and encourage me when I was struggling with studying English. My homestay host helped me improve my English and supported me throughout my experience in Canada. Saki English for Academic Purposes Top 12 reasons to choose QSoE 1 One of the top 5 Universities in Canada 2 Small class sizes 3 CEFR benchmarking for each level 4 Courses appear on official transcripts 5 Our commitment to SDGs 6 Volunteer Club 7 A safe place to learn 8 Natural beauty 9 Competitive Tuition Fees 10 No application or placement fees 11 National scholarships 12 Student experience Top 12 reasons to choose QSoE One of the top 5 Universities in Canada Small class sizes CEFR benchmarking for each level Courses appear on official transcripts Our commitment to SDGs Volunteer Club A safe place to learn Natural beauty Competitive Tuition Fees No application or placement fees National scholarships Student experience Contact us Faculty of Education Queen's University Duncan McArthur Hall Room B242, 511 Union Street Kingston, Ontario, Canada K7M 5R7 1-613-533-2472 qsoe@queensu.ca Follow us on social media Queen's Privacy Statement ©2026 Queen's University"
    },
