Procedure Academic Policies & Non-Academic Policies LLM Students Program Graduates - Join the Alumni Network Clinics Queen's Legal Aid Prison Law Clinic Business Law Clinic Elder Law Clinic Family Law Clinic Moot Court Program Public Interest Internships Pro Bono Students Canada Law Journals Student Support Education & Equity Academic Consideration & Academic Accommodation Costs & Financial Assistance Awards Student Financial Aid Impact Report Equity, Diversity, Inclusivity and Indigeneity Community Outreach Queen's Law Fall Classic Academic Program Course Information Course Information Master Law Course Catalogue Timetable Exam Schedule Sessional Dates Academic Integrity Jurisdiction Process for Instructors and Students Forms Contact Information Academic Calendar Career Development Combined Degrees BCom/JD JD/MBA JD/MPA MA(Econ)/JD JD/MIR Civil / Common Breadcrumb Queen's Law Programs JD Student Experience International Exchanges Partnered Universities Koç University Faculty of Law Koç University Koç University was founded in 1993 as a non-profit private university in Istanbul, Türkiye. In the twenty years since its establishment, Koç University has become one of the leading universities in Türkiye, distinguished by notable contributions to the elevation of education, knowledge and service both domestically and beyond. With Colleges of Social Sciences and Humanities, Administrative Sciences and Economics, Science, Engineering, Law, Nursing and Medicine, Koç University offers 22 undergraduate, 32 graduate and 18 Ph.D. programs. Its beautiful campus is situated on a sixty-two-acre estate that succeeds in balancing accessibility to all of Istanbul with a retreat from the distractions of city life. The product of a meticulous, integrated design, Koç University’s sixty buildings -academic and administrative- include laboratories, libraries, dormitories, faculty residences, social venues, health centers and sports facilities. Koç University Law School aims to nurture creative and sophisticated lawyers with its content-rich courses in public law, private law, and international law. In law school, at least 30% of the courses, especially courses with international law content are taught in English. See Course Descriptions (link is external) . Fact Sheet 2024/25 (link is external) Koç University Faculty of Law (link is external) Koc University International Office Facebook page (link is external) Sessional Dates Fall term – early September to mid-January (including examination period) Winter term (called Spring Term) February to early June, including the examination period. Faculty of Law Queen's University 128 Union Street Kingston ON K7L 3N6 Canada Telephone 613.533.6000 Facebook (link is external) Instagram (link is external) Twitter (link is external) twitter (link is external) LinkedIn (link is external) Sound cloud (link is external) Queen's University Wordmark Footer Privacy (link is external) Credits Queen's University is situated on traditional Anishinaabe and Haudenosaunee Territory. © 2026 Queen's Law. All Rights Reserved."
