      "description": "Page not found | Department of Geography and Planning Cookie Disclosure Queen's University uses cookies to provide the best possible online experience. Learn about our privacy practices. OK Skip to main content Skip to footer Sign In University Wide MyQueen’sU - SOLUS, MyHR, and more Microsoft 365 Outlook on the web - Email onQ Research–Service Portal: Cayuse and TRAQ Course Reserves Web Proxy Change password / Manage NetID Faculty/School Portals Business - Program Portals Grad Studies – Faculty and Staff Portal Health Sciences - Elentra Law - QLaw Smith Engineering Intranet Geography and Planning Main navigation Home Undergraduate Down arrow Programs Courses Research Department Student Council (DSC) Graduate Down arrow Programs Courses Funding and Awards Completed Theses Graduate Student Council (GSC) Planning Down arrow Overview SURP Down arrow Local and Regional Planning Down arrow Overview City of Toronto City of Montréal City of Ottawa City of Kingston National and International Outreach Down arrow Overview Ambassadors' Forum China Projects Office National Executive Forum on Public Property International Experience Opportunities Program of Study Down arrow Overview Combined Degrees Project Courses Internship Program Courses & Timetables Important Forms Admissions Funding & Awards Down arrow Overview Awards & Scholarship Deadlines Corporate Scholarships International Travel Awards OPPI & CPI Awards Other Fellowship Awards SURP Awards Alumni Spotlight Graduate Association SURP Annual Reports SURP Master's Theses and Reports SURP Newsletters Community Life Planning As a Career Program Objectives SURP History Research People Down arrow Administration Faculty Adjuncts Graduate Students & Postdoctoral Fellows Search I-EDIAA Contact System Page not found Page not found The requested page could not be found. Department of Geography and Planning Mackintosh-Corry Hall, E208 Queen's University Kingston, ON K7L 3N9 Canada Tel: (613) 533-6030 Quick Links Contact Us Faculty of Arts and Science School of Graduate Studies and Postdoctoral Affairs Visit Queen's Give to Geography and Planning Web Privacy Queen’s University is situated on the territory of the Haudenosaunee and Anishinaabek . © 2026 Queen’s University"
