ted with Research Learn more about starting your research About Us Toggle submenu About Us Overview Governance Staff Directory Featured Collections News Careers Policies Giving close Close menu Menu chat Ask us Search Search close Search Search close Utility Menu accessibility Accessibility keyboard_arrow_down Library Accessibility Services Adaptive Technology Centre person My Account keyboard_arrow_down My Library Account Online Resource Access OnQ search Search keyboard_arrow_down Main navigation Search Tools keyboard_arrow_down Search Tools Overview Omni Databases Journals QSpace Google Scholar Archives (AtoM) Digital Collections Types of Information Data & Statistics Geospatial Data Government Information Maps & Air Photos Newspapers Rare Books & Special Collections Theses & Dissertations Video Collections Virtual Exhibits View All ... Use the Library keyboard_arrow_down Use the Library Overview Locations & Hours Bracken Health Sciences Library Douglas Library Education Library Jordan Special Collections Joseph S. Stauffer Library Lederman Law Library Queen's Archives Watson Hall LINQ Featured Spaces Study Rooms Borrowing Request Materials Library Accessibility Services Technology Classrooms Print, Scan, Copy Research Support keyboard_arrow_down Research Overview Copyright Advisory Office Research Data Management Scholarly Publishing Teach & Learn keyboard_arrow_down Teach & Learn Overview Course Reserves Exams & Syllabi Open Education Resources Library Indigenous Resources Portal Help & How-To keyboard_arrow_down Help & How-To Overview User Guides Undergraduate Students Graduate Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Community How-To Topics Ask Us Frequently Asked Questions Library Department Guides Archives & Special Collections Copyright Advisory Office Digital Initiatives & Open Scholarship Education Engineering & Science GIS, Maps, and Government Information Health Sciences Humanities, Business & Social Sciences Law Subject Research Guides About Us keyboard_arrow_down About Us Overview Governance Staff Directory Featured Collections News Careers Policies Giving Breadcrumb Home About Us Careers Careers Introduction Come work with us! The library offers rewarding work through which people can fully realize their professional and academic aspirations. Queen's offers competitive salaries and a full range of benefits and pension coverage. We are committed to employment equity and diversity in the workplace and welcome applications from individuals from equity-deserving groups such as women, racialized/visible minorities, Indigenous/Aboriginal peoples, persons with a disability, persons who identify in the LGBTQ+ community and others who reflect the diversity of Canadian society. Queen’s University Library is part of the larger Queen’s community, a university with a reputation for quality, excellence, and global reach. The library is an excellent and welcoming space that offers a creative, engaging, and rewarding work environment. We pride ourselves in collaboration and foster a supportive and inclusive workplace by weaving fairness, accessibility, and equity into the fabric of everything that we do. With staff and students from a diverse range of backgrounds, you will find a team of enthusiastic, inspiring, and supportive colleagues who are passionate about making information and sources available to a diverse group of users. Competitive (attractive) salary and benefits, career development opportunities, and work-life balance are just some of the benefits of working at Queen’s University Library. This page is for Queen's University Faculty Association (QUFA) Librarian & Archivist positions. For current Library Work Study opportunities, please see the Queen's Work Study Program page . Be sure to check our website, social media accounts, and the Queen's University Careers page regularly for new staff postings. If you have any questions, please send an email to library.hr@queensu.ca . Research and Instruction Librarian, Business & Social Sciences (Initial Continuing Track Appointment) Posted on: March 23, 2026 Apply by: April 19, 2026 Status: In progress Research and Instruction Librarian, Business and Social Sciences PD (PDF) Research and Instruction Librarian, Business and Social Sciences Posting (PDF) Business & Social Sciences Librarian (Initial Continuing Track Appointment) Posted on: June 10, 2025 Apply by: July 21, 2025 Status: Closed Business & Social Sciences Librarian Job Posting (PDF 129 KB) Business & Social Sciences Librarian Position Guide (PDF 226 KB) Research Data Management Librarian (Special Appointment) Posted on: November 28, 2024 Apply by: January 7, 2025 Status: Closed Research Data Management Librarian –  Job Posting (PDF 140 KB) Research Data Management Librarian – Position Guide (PDF 77 KB) Metadata & Discovery Librarian - Cataloguing (Limited-Term Appointment) Posted on: July 24, 2024 Apply by: August 13, 2024 Status: Closed Metadata & Discovery Librarian Job Posting (PDF 162 KB) Metadata & Discovery Librarian Position Guide (PDF 129 KB) forum Chat chat Ask Us Locations Bracken Health Sciences Library Douglas Library Education Library Jordan Special Collections Lederman Law Library Stauffer Library Queen's Archives Watson Hall LINQ Featured Spaces Departments Archives & Special Collections Copyright Advisory Office Digital Initiatives & Open Scholarship Education Engineering & Science Health Sciences Humanities, Business & Social Sciences Law Queens Library Logo Footer menu Accessibility Careers FAQs Staff Directory Support your library Privacy Statement Youtube Instagram X © Copyright Queen's University Library Kingston, Ontario, Canada Queen's University is situated on the territory of the Haudenosaunee and Anishinaabek"
